KNOWNBUG ([expr.prim.lambda]/3-7): a lambda expression has a unique closure
*class* type with a public inline operator() (the body) and -- for a captureless
lambda -- a non-explicit conversion to a pointer-to-function.  A closure is an
object, not a function pointer, so it can be stored by value in a type-erasing
wrapper such as std::function.  CBMC models a captureless lambda as a bare
function pointer, so std::function constructed from a lambda stores a function
pointer rather than a closure object and the type-erased call dereferences a
null pointer.  Reclassify CORE once a lambda is a closure object that
std::function stores and invokes.
